plain = 128x128 identity stack (our own baseline, NOT FlexAttention).
per-layer = permute/invert around every attention -- the pessimistic bound.
once = permute at the input, run the stack in permuted space, invert once --
       what NOTES sec 4 assumes and sec 5 flags as argued rather than measured.
If the two columns converge as depth grows, the amortisation claim holds.

