READ THIS AS p(BQ, A, MASK), NOT p(BQ, A). exp0 measured a 1.61x
small-tile penalty at CONSTANT element count -- but the permuted
kernel at the same 16x16 tile delivered only 66% of its predicted
gain, and the tile shape was held fixed there, so occupancy alone
does not explain it. The likely mechanism is that per-CTA fixed
cost (Q tile load, softmax init and epilogue) is amortised over
FEWER tiles when the mask is sparser, so the penalty grows as work
per program shrinks. If that is right, p varies across masks at a
FIXED tile shape and a 2-D correction table is under-specified.
Compare the same tile row across the four masks to find out.

